# Sample `oslc:Error` alerts -- the local stand-in for redpencil's error graph.
#
# Loaded into the named graph <http://mu.semte.ch/graphs/errors> by the
# `triplestore` service in the dishacled docker-compose stack, so alert
# ingestion (A1) and visualisation (A2) can be built and tested with no
# dependency on the live feed. See docs/alert-fixture.md.
#
# Every alert here conforms to <http://lblod.data.gift/shapes/ErrorShape>, the
# shape the threshold-monitor processor publishes; that shape lives in
# contracts.ttl and is checked against this file by tests/test_alert_fixture.py.
#
# Two things about this data are deliberate:
#
#   * Alerts are IRIs, not blank nodes. The processor emits a blank node today
#     (src/index.ts: `const id = blankNode()`), but lblod's own consumer
#     retrieves an alert by URI (`VALUES ?uri { ... }`) and the processor's own
#     README example writes an IRI. A blank node is not addressable, so it
#     could not be linked to or deep-linked from a UI. See
#     docs/toolchain-open-questions.md section 5.
#   * The last alert carries neither `oslc:largePreview` nor `dct:references`.
#     Both are optional in the shape, so a consumer that assumes they are
#     always present is wrong -- this alert is what makes that a test failure
#     rather than a production surprise.
#
# The messages follow the demonstrator's cm/mm story: a threshold monitor
# watching centimetre and millimetre measurement streams.

@prefix oslc:   <http://open-services.net/ns/core#> .
@prefix mu:     <http://mu.semte.ch/vocabularies/core/> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix alert:  <https://dishacled.github.io/demo/alerts/> .
@prefix member: <https://dishacled.github.io/demo/members/> .
@prefix agent:  <https://dishacled.github.io/demo/agents#> .


# 1 -- centimetre reading above the configured maximum, full detail.
alert:2f8c1d94-5a3b-4e7f-9c21-6b0d8e4a1f37
  a oslc:Error ;
  mu:uuid "2f8c1d94-5a3b-4e7f-9c21-6b0d8e4a1f37" ;
  dct:subject "threshold-monitor" ;
  oslc:message "Measurement above maximum threshold" ;
  dct:created "2026-07-15T09:21:45.725Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  dct:creator agent:threshold-monitor ;
  oslc:largePreview "Member <https://dishacled.github.io/demo/members/m-0417> has value 412.5 cm, above the configured maximum of 300 cm." ;
  dct:references member:m-0417 .


# 2 -- millimetre reading below the configured minimum, a different stream.
alert:8b41e2a7-0c96-4d58-b3ea-17f5c9d02e64
  a oslc:Error ;
  mu:uuid "8b41e2a7-0c96-4d58-b3ea-17f5c9d02e64" ;
  dct:subject "threshold-monitor" ;
  oslc:message "Measurement below minimum threshold" ;
  dct:created "2026-07-15T11:04:02.118Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  dct:creator agent:threshold-monitor ;
  oslc:largePreview "Member <https://dishacled.github.io/demo/members/m-0418> has value 42.0 mm, below the configured minimum of 100 mm." ;
  dct:references member:m-0418 .


# 3 -- centimetre breach again, later, so alerts can be ordered and grouped.
alert:c05a7f63-9e12-4b8d-a4c7-3d61b28e5091
  a oslc:Error ;
  mu:uuid "c05a7f63-9e12-4b8d-a4c7-3d61b28e5091" ;
  dct:subject "threshold-monitor" ;
  oslc:message "Measurement above maximum threshold" ;
  dct:created "2026-07-16T06:47:30.902Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  dct:creator agent:threshold-monitor ;
  oslc:largePreview "Member <https://dishacled.github.io/demo/members/m-0503> has value 356.8 cm, above the configured maximum of 300 cm." ;
  dct:references member:m-0503 .


# 4 -- both optional properties absent. Consumers must handle this.
alert:47d9b0e5-6a28-4c31-8f5b-92e0a7c46d13
  a oslc:Error ;
  mu:uuid "47d9b0e5-6a28-4c31-8f5b-92e0a7c46d13" ;
  dct:subject "threshold-monitor" ;
  oslc:message "Measurement outside configured bounds" ;
  dct:created "2026-07-16T08:15:11.443Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  dct:creator agent:threshold-monitor .
